      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "content": "### How to read this test\n\nRun `run-traffic-response-test.ps1` to send **50 RPS → 300 RPS → 50 RPS** traffic. The first panel compares actual incoming traffic with the one-minute observation used by the current calculator. If the observed line rises after the spike and falls after recovery with delay, that is the averaging lag we are going to improve. The second panel shows how that delay reaches the applied PASS rate.\n\nAll algorithm gauges are tagged only by `strategy`, never by campaign ID, so adding this dashboard does not create an unbounded Prometheus time-series count.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Test guide",
      "type": "text"
